Z||000004||batboy||12-01-1999||04:19 PM||||I bet they're talking about V8 Archie's Fiero list. Yeah, from what I saw briefly last spring when I checked it out, a lot of those guys must think their own guano don't stink. You know the kind, the financially well off that rarely get their own hands dirty. They have mega-bucks into their garage-baby show cars and look down on the rest of us working slobs with average Fieros.<P>Their moderator is quite often the little dictator sometimes. It's one thing to control a discussion in your own home, but a whole different story trying to control an open forum discussion over the internet. Personally, I see nothing wrong in discussing controversal issues and/or disagreeing with others in a rational manner, as long as there is no personal attacks or name calling involved.||||reg||1
Z||000005||RossT||12-02-1999||12:33 AM||||I do not understand the mentality that some of those with the show cars have.  I use to <BR>own a 68 plymouth barracuda as my daily driver. At car shows, many with show cars would not even come over to look at what I had. But I really love that car.  Now I own<BR>one of the low mileage fieros, and I am very jealous of those that use theirs as daily drivers.  Every time I see a daily driver fiero in my town I go out of my way to check it out and talk to the owner. My car just sits in the garage with a cover on it. Scared to death just to drive (might get a scratch). My next fiero will be a daily driver.<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||12-02-1999||07:15 AM||||I've often thought about what I'd do if I had a realy low mileage Fiero.  I'm not sure if I'd park it or drive it.  I think I'd be inclined to drive and enjoy it for what it is, a fun car to drive.  Not sure though.  Actually I don't see me ever being faced with that dilema anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DJRice||12-02-1999||09:57 AM||||I have quit driving mine as much because it recently reached 140k, but I still drive it at least once a week.  I just cant let it sit for too long.  They are just too fun to drive.  Gotta get my fix of that 6 cyl growl!||||reg||1
Z||000008||ChadMan||12-02-1999||01:02 PM||||Ideally I'd like to have one "show" Fiero and one daily-driver Fiero.  That way I'd have the best of both worlds.  <P>I don't blame you for not driving your low-mile car, Ross - the general public is just too dumb, mean and inconsiderate to be trusted with a gem like that.  My 88 Coupe was egged two months ago and I was mad enough to murder.  I can only imagine how much madder I'd be if it were a nice low-mileage GT.||||reg||1
